        "id": 334214,
        "name": "Melodie",
        "summary": "Melodie was a rhythm-based platform game for the PSP in development at Kuju Entertainment's Brighton studios in 2005. While it never saw an actual release, a prototype was found in a PSP development kit and released on the internet in 2016.\n\nThe prototype included a small selection of music:\n\n- Annie - Chewing Gum\n- Beastie Boys - Intergalactic\n- Bloodhound Gang - The Bad Touch\n- The Chemical Brothers - Galvanize\n- Kylie Minogue - Slow\n- Public Enemy - She Watch Channel Zero\n\nThe actual gameplay has elements generated from and timed to the selected music track, including level decorations and a procedurally-generated \"Creature\" for the player to race.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coa0sr.jpg",
